  "limitations_and_external_availability": [
    "The canonical runs reused one retained source-audited local-node tuple with fresh actor state and unspent deterministic inputs; this is not a cold clean-host reproduction.",
    "Cold provisioning can require crates and Rust distributions, the exact Docker image digest, Logos circuits v0.4.2, and pinned source artifacts from external registries or GitHub; outages can block setup but cannot relax identity checks.",
    "An initial deployer build without RAPIDSNARK_LIB_DIR entered the upstream GitHub release fallback and failed before chain mutation because unzip was unavailable; the successful deployment used four locally hash-verified Rapisnark/GMP libraries.",
    "Literal loopback isolates access but does not emulate public peer propagation, provider quotas, organic timing, fee markets, or public testnet behavior.",
    "Public deployment, public execution, and public recording are intentionally deferred under ADR 0023 and must not be inferred from this packet.",
    "Composed actual-node refund, restart, reorg, concurrency, chaos, and production-readiness expansion remain owner-gated phases under ADR 0027.",
    "The run-recorded no-public-resource assertion is supported by deterministic_local route configuration but was not independently packet-captured.",
    "Private actor roots and shared devnet containers remain deliberately retained for audit; only role sidecar cleanup is claimed."
